Security + robustness hardening from code review

Deleted dead code: SystemService.dockerVersion(), NetworkService.dockerNetworks()/
dockerNetworkInspect() (duplicates of DockerService), shqArgs().

Fixed:
- backup.schedule: shell injection via job `name` in the generated cron script,
  path traversal in script/archive placement, and newline-split crontab lines;
  `name` is now strict ^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$, `cron` validated as exactly 5 fields,
  and grep -vF (fixed-string) replaces the regex grep.
- backup.create: posix.basename() on the archive name (no ../ traversal).
- sshExecutor: cached in-flight connect() promise (no double-connect race),
  persistent close/error handlers reset `connected` so a dropped connection
  reconnects instead of crashing on an unhandled "error" event, exec timeout
  now KILLs and closes the channel (no leak) with an honest "remote op may
  still be running" message, and stream-level errors are handled.
- hostKey pinning: compare fingerprints padding-stripped so standard
  `ssh-keygen -lf` output pins successfully.
- server: SIGINT/SIGTERM now closes transports/HTTP server and exits (was
  hanging); /mcp refuses non-loopback binds without UGNAS_HTTP_ALLOW_REMOTE=1
  (transport is unauthenticated); readJsonBody capped at 1 MiB.

Improvements:
- planOrExecute cross-checks the confirming call's payload against the plan-time
  payload (payloadMismatch) — stale tokens with different arguments are rejected.
- BusyBox portability: cached GNU ls/find capability probes; files.list falls
  back to `ls -1p` (+ parseLsPlain) and files.find to `stat -c '%s|%Y|%n'` when
  GNU flags are missing; files.list errors on nonexistent paths instead of [].
- system.pools parsers rebuilt against real tool output: vgs/lvs/pvs with '|'
  separator (three sections), btrfs `path /dev/...` device lines with
  label-quote stripping, lsblk -P KEY="value" pairs (blank columns survive).
- files.thumbnail now gates its LOCAL file write behind the confirm token
  (NAS-side render/base64 fetch remain pre-gate; only /tmp temp involved).
- tests/wiring.test.ts: asserts the exact 39-tool registration set, that every
  contract service method is a function, and that confirmToken field presence
  matches each tool's mutating status.

Typecheck clean; 35/35 tests; build + stdio/HTTP smoke pass (39 tools).